  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is placed on a smooth horizontal surface and it is pulled by a light spring as shown in the diagram. If the ends A and B of the spring are moving with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively and the rate at which spring energy is increasing is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. then what is the value of spring force (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>)?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0022_38ea40d60ea5.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 287px; height: 103px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, distance moved by A and B in any time interval as measured from natural length of spring are xA and xB respectively. Let, <math> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </math> is the natural length of spring, then elongation in spring at any instant is<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext>x</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext>x</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>U</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>kx</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow><mfrac><mrow><mtext>dU</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dt</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dt</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>kx&#160;</mtext> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>v</mtext> <mtext>A</mtext> </msub> <mo>-</mo> <msub> <mtext>v</mtext> <mtext>B</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo> <mtext>kx</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0&#160;</mn> <mtext>N</mtext> </mrow> </math>"
  }
